  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $3w+2=2w+2$\n- $4w-7=4w-7$\n- $6w+5=6w+9$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3w+2 & =2w+2 \\\\ 3w+2-2w-2 & =2w+2-2w-2 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3w+2=2w+2$ has the unique solution $w=0.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4w-7 & =4w-7 \\\\ 4w-7-4w & =4w-7-4w \\\\ -7 & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6w+5 & =6w+9 \\\\ 6w+5-6w & =6w+9-6w \\\\ 5 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $6w+5=6w+9$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
